Begin your reply with the resolution line — it is required, and a reply without it
is refused:

  resolution: <change|investigation|experiment|decision>

Choose deliberately. `investigation` answers a question without shipping code,
`experiment` tests the riskiest assumption with an instrumented surface, and
`decision` records a choice — often not to build — and closes on a written ADR.
`change` is a legitimate answer arrived at quickly; it is not a legitimate default
arrived at silently.

Then outline the concrete steps to reach it, and name the proof the resolution will
have to carry to close.
